# Inventory: costing and reversal

Status: internally checked illustration; no paid review requested. Related
requirements MC07, MC19, MC20; gaps G4, G7, G12.

## Proposed treatment and checked consequence

For interchangeable goods outside the special scope exclusions, apply one
consistent FIFO or weighted-average formula to inventories of similar nature
and use under the inspected IAS-equivalent text. The same purchases (10 units
at 5, then 10 at 7) and sale of 12 give:

| Formula | Cost of sales | Closing stock |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| FIFO | 64 | 56 |
| LIFO illustration/company-policy profile | 80 | 40 |
| Periodic weighted average | 72 | 48 |

All three account for the same total cost 120. Their differing closing values
cannot be removed by relabelling concepts. Under the inspected IAS-equivalent
reversal rule, cost 56 and net realisable value 50 produce an expense of 6.
If the original conditions reverse and NRV rises to 54, restore 4. If NRV rises
to 60, restore only 6, leaving carrying value 56. The original cost and prior
write-down must therefore remain in state.

The [calculation report](../accounting-dossier-checks.json) checks these amounts
and the cap. It does not decide whether an actual inventory population is
interchangeable or whether a particular NRV estimate is justified.

